7.Application

16.SUBNETTING
ifconfig -a /ip addr show(new)- command to display network details
192.168.1.0/24 - CIDR format
NAT - Network Adress translation
ARP(Address Resolution Protocol) -  find the missing information, it broadcasts an ARP request on the local network, asking which device has the target IP address
RIP (Routing Information Protocol)- distance vector protocol finding best connection basic on:
Periodic Updates: RIP broadcasts its entire routing table to all neighbors every 30 seconds.
Hop Count Limit: To prevent routing loops and control network traffic, RIP enforces a maximum hop count of 15. Any route that requires 16 hops is considered unreachable.
OSPF (Open Shortest Path First) - updates INFORMATIONS to neighboring routes, dont have hop limit
AS (Autonomous System) - IS large network or a group of networks managed by a single administrative entity
BGP (border gateway protocol) - doesn't find a path; it makes policy decisions to find the best path based on rules configured by network administrators, ensuring efficient and reliable data exchange across the global internet.

